---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_HREF } from '../consts';

const title = 'AI & Content-Usage Policy — Lookout';
const description =
  'How AI systems may use Lookout: answer engines are welcome to read and cite the site; use for AI/ML training or dataset creation is reserved. Read the policy and how to license.';

const channels = [
  { channel: 'robots.txt', where: '/robots.txt', what: 'Allows general search and AI answer/search agents; disallows named AI training & dataset crawlers.' },
  { channel: 'TDM Reservation Protocol (W3C)', where: '/.well-known/tdmrep.json', what: 'tdm-reservation: 1 for the whole site — text & data mining rights reserved, referenced by EU CDSM Art. 4 & the EU AI Act.' },
  { channel: 'AIPREF (IETF)', where: 'Content-Usage response header', what: 'train-ai=n, search=y — training declined, search permitted.' },
  { channel: 'noai / noimageai', where: 'X-Robots-Tag response header', what: 'Publisher AI-training opt-out. Carries no noindex — search indexing stays required.' },
  { channel: 'ai.txt', where: '/ai.txt', what: 'Human- and machine-readable summary of this policy.' },
  { channel: 'llms.txt', where: '/llms.txt', what: 'A curated overview to help assistants describe and cite Lookout accurately. Grants no training rights.' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-balance text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">AI &amp; content-usage policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-pretty text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      Lookout is built to be found, quoted, and recommended by AI assistants — and to keep its written content out of the
      datasets used to train them. This page explains, plainly, what AI systems may and may not do with our site content,
      and how to license it.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated 7 July 2026 · Applies to all of <strong class="text-slate-300">lookout.dosanjhlabs.com</strong></p>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/[0.06] p-6">
      <p class="text-slate-200"><strong class="text-white">In one line:</strong> AI search and answer engines are <strong class="text-white">welcome to read, index, and cite</strong> Lookout to help people find us. Using our site content to <strong class="text-white">train, fine-tune, or build datasets/RAG corpora</strong> for AI models is <strong class="text-white">reserved</strong> and requires a license.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/15 bg-emerald-500/[0.04] p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-white">✓ Welcomed</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">Reading and indexing our pages, answering a user's question from them, quoting short passages <strong class="text-slate-200">with a link back to the source</strong>, and surfacing Lookout in AI-powered search. This drives people to a monitoring tool that solves a real problem — exactly what we want.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/15 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-white">⚠ Reserved</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">Automated collection of our site content for <strong class="text-slate-200">AI/ML model training, fine-tuning, distillation, embedding-index or RAG-corpus building, or any dataset creation</strong> — whether by a crawler, an API, or a third-party dataset. Not permitted without a written license.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-black text-white">Why we draw the line here</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-pretty leading-relaxed text-slate-300">
      The copy on this site — the product explanations, the docs, the FAQ answers — is original work, written to help people
      understand and run Lookout. We publish it openly so anyone can evaluate the product, and we're glad when an assistant
      points someone here. But large-scale ingestion of that writing into a training set, where it's absorbed, un-attributed,
      and resold as a model's own output, is a different act entirely. We reserve it. This keeps referral traffic flowing
      while protecting the writing that makes Lookout worth citing.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
      This is a policy about the <strong class="text-slate-300">marketing site's written content</strong>, not about Lookout's
      application source code. The agent and control plane are published separately under the
      <strong class="text-slate-300">Apache License 2.0</strong> — see the project repository for terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-black text-white">How this policy is expressed (machine-readable)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400">The same reservation is declared through every current standard so automated agents can honor it without guessing:</p>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900/40">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[36rem] border-collapse text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/10 text-left">
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-300">Channel</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-300">Where</th>
            <th class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-slate-300">What it says</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {channels.map((c) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-white/5 last:border-b-0 align-top">
              <td class="px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white">{c.channel}</td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-indigo-300"><code>{c.where}</code></td>
              <td class="px-5 py-3 text-slate-400">{c.what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-black text-white">Agents we welcome vs. decline</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400">Our <a class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300" href="/robots.txt">robots.txt</a> is the authoritative list. In summary:</p>
    <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-white">Welcomed (answer / search)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">General search engines (Googlebot, Bingbot, DuckDuckBot), and AI answer/search agents including <strong class="text-slate-200">OAI-SearchBot</strong> &amp; <strong class="text-slate-200">ChatGPT-User</strong> (OpenAI), <strong class="text-slate-200">Claude-SearchBot</strong> &amp; <strong class="text-slate-200">Claude-User</strong> (Anthropic), <strong class="text-slate-200">PerplexityBot</strong> &amp; <strong class="text-slate-200">Perplexity-User</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Applebot</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">DuckAssistBot</strong>, and Amazon's / Meta's / Mistral's search-and-user agents — all of which cite and link back.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-slate-900/40 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-white">Declined (training / dataset)</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">Training and dataset crawlers including <strong class="text-slate-200">GPTBot</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">ClaudeBot</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Google-Extended</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Applebot-Extended</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Meta-ExternalAgent</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">CCBot</strong> (Common Crawl), <strong class="text-slate-200">Bytespider</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Amazonbot</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">cohere-ai</strong>, <strong class="text-slate-200">Diffbot</strong>, and other dataset/scraper bots. <span class="text-slate-500">Google-Extended and Applebot-Extended are training opt-outs only — blocking them does not affect Google or Apple search.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-14 text-2xl font-black text-white">Licensing</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400">Want to use Lookout's site content in a training set, an evaluation benchmark, a retrieval corpus, or another product? That's often possible under license. Reach out and tell us what you have in mind.</p>
    <a href={CONTACT_HREF} class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-r from-indigo-500 to-fuchsia-500 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white shadow-lg shadow-indigo-500/25 transition hover:opacity-90">Contact us about licensing →</a>

    <div class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02] p-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
      Content on this site is © 2026 Jasvant Dosanjh / Dosanjh Labs. All rights reserved except as licensed. Nothing here is legal advice.
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
